Voters' Minds, Quinnipiac University New York State Poll Finds; Senator Chuck Schumer's Job Approval: 36%", "source": "Quinnipiac University Poll", "published": "2026-09-23T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTFBkUlZyekpsX0pqMm4tclpVdlFFOUoyaXZNWFVBczRCVDE5NGY4WWZ0LVBNRnd0bEx3NmtwOGF3MVJ5NUZVVkJhQzI3WVh1aVlWSW55WnRfVzhLZnM?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 14.12, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 11.83, "poll_sd": 4.86, "poll_weight": 0.55, "fundamentals": {"margin": 14.31, "lean": 6.0, "environment": 4.2, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.11}, "rating_margin": 14.0, "sigma_race": 4.5, "sigma_total": 5.01, "baseline_margin": 12.87, "analyst_adjustment": -0.87, "key_factors": ["Hochul leads by 11-12 points in recent high-quality polls (Emerson, Marist, Quinnipiac)", "All seven expert ratings put the race at Likely D or better", "Prediction markets price Hochul at 95-97%", "Blakeman's strength with independents noted in Marist polling, but not enough to close the gap"], "rationale": "Recent polls from Emerson, Marist and Quinnipiac consistently show Hochul ahead by double digits, and every major rater and all three prediction markets treat her as a heavy favorite. Blakeman's edge with independents and Trump's upstate rally are the main upside scenarios for Republicans, but the polling breadth makes an upset unlikely.", "watch": "A further erosion of Hochul's standing with independent and upstate voters could tighten the race toward Likely D territory.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Kathy Hochul seeks a full term against Nassau County executive Bruce Blakeman in a state that leans Democratic by about eight points. Polling throughout the fall has been consistent: Emerson shows Hochul up 12, Marist up 11, and Quinnipiac up 19, with an overall average near 12 points. Every major race rater places New York in the Solid or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets price Hochul's chances at 95 percent or higher.\n\nBlakeman has kept the race competitive on paper, raising over $13 million and running strongest with independent voters, and President Trump campaigned with him in upstate New York in October. Still, Hochul holds an incumbency and fundraising edge, and the polling breadth leaves little evidence of a genuine toss-up. The race remains safely in Hochul's column, with the main question being the final margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9761, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9756, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9778, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9804, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9805, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9817, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9752, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9892, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.0}]}